# Cursor Editor — Model Provider Configuration

## Overview

Cursor's model provider system determines which AI models power each interaction mode (Chat, Agent, Tab). Users can configure built-in providers (OpenAI, Anthropic), custom endpoints (OpenAI-compatible servers, local models), and select different models per mode. This system is fundamental to Cursor's functionality — every AI interaction routes through this provider configuration.

Provider configuration is accessible through **Cursor Settings > Model Provider** in the editor UI.

---

## Built-in Providers

### OpenAI

| Model | Capability | Recommended For |
|-------|-----------|-----------------|
| GPT-4 / GPT-4 Turbo | General-purpose reasoning, code generation | Chat, Agent mode |
| GPT-4o | Multimodal (text, images) | Complex code explanations with screenshots |
| GPT-3.5 Turbo | Faster, lighter tasks | Quick edits, Tab autocompletions |

**Configuration**: Enter your OpenAI API key. Model selection is per-mode (Chat, Agent, Tab).

### Anthropic (Claude)

| Model | Capability | Recommended For |
|-------|-----------|-----------------|
| Claude Opus | Deep reasoning, complex code architecture | Agent mode, heavy refactoring |
| Claude Sonnet | Balanced performance and speed | Chat, Tab, most workflows |
| Claude Haiku | Fast, lightweight tasks | Tab autocompletions, quick suggestions |

**Configuration**: Enter your Anthropic API key. Models are selected per mode in Cursor Settings.

### Cursor's Built-in Models

Cursor also provides its own hosted models through the default configuration:

| Model ID | Description | SDK Equivalent |
|----------|-------------|---------------|
| `composer-2.5` | Current default for most integrations | `model: { id: "composer-2.5" }` |
| `auto` | Server-picks the best model | `model: "auto"` (Python) / `{ id: "auto" }` (TypeScript) |

