## Custom Endpoints

Custom endpoints allow you to use any OpenAI-compatible API server. This is useful for:

- **Local models** (Ollama, vLLM, llama.cpp)
- **Self-hosted inference servers**
- **Proxy servers** (LiteLLM, OpenRouter, Together AI)
- **Private enterprise models**

### Configuring Custom Endpoints

1. Open Cursor Settings
2. Navigate to Model Provider section
3. Select "Custom" or "OpenAI Compatible" provider type
4. Enter the following:

```
Base URL: http://localhost:11434/v1          # Ollama
Base URL: http://localhost:8080/v1           # vLLM
Base URL: https://api.openrouter.ai/v1       # OpenRouter
Base URL: https://your-enterprise-api.com/v1 # Enterprise proxy
```

5. Enter API key (or leave blank if your server doesn't require one)

### Local Model Configuration (Ollama)

```json
{
  "cursor.agent.model": {
    "provider": "custom",
    "baseUrl": "http://localhost:11434/v1",
    "apiKey": "",
    "modelId": "codellama:7b",
    "mode": {
      "chat": "codellama:7b",
      "agent": "codellama:13b",
      "tab": "codellama:7b"
    }
  }
}
```

### Ollama Quick Start

```bash
# Install Ollama
brew install ollama        # macOS
# or on Windows, download from ollama.com

# Pull a model
ollama pull codellama

# Run the Ollama server (default: localhost:11434)
ollama serve
```

Then configure Cursor with base URL `http://localhost:11434/v1`.

### vLLM Quick Start

```bash
# Install vLLM
pip install vllm

# Start a server serving a model
vllm serve meta-llama/Llama-2-7b-chat-hf --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080
```

Then configure Cursor with base URL `http://localhost:8080/v1`.

