## Model Selection Per Mode

Cursor allows different models for different interaction modes:

| Mode | Purpose | Typical Model Choice |
|------|---------|---------------------|
| **Chat** | Conversational Q&A, explanations | Sonnet / GPT-4 (balanced quality) |
| **Agent** | Code modification, file edits, tool execution | Opus / GPT-4 Turbo (max reasoning) |
| **Tab** | Inline code completions | Haiku / GPT-3.5 / smaller local model (speed) |

### Configuration Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Cursor Settings] --> B[Model Provider Tab]
    B --> C[Select Provider]
    C --> D[Enter API Key]
    D --> E[Configure Per-Mode Models]
    E --> F[Chat Model: Select]
    E --> G[Agent Model: Select]
    E --> H[Tab Model: Select]
    F --> I[Save]
    G --> I
    H --> I
    I --> J[Provider Active]
```

### Why Different Models Per Mode

- **Chat** requires good conversational ability — moderate model size
- **Agent** performs code modifications with tool use — needs strong reasoning
- **Tab** must respond in milliseconds — needs speed over capability

Using the same model for all modes wastes resources on Tab (too slow) or limits Agent capability (too weak).

