## Provider Routing

Cursor routes requests to providers based on the interaction mode:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[User Interaction] --> B{What type?}
    B -->|Chat message| C[Chat Model Provider]
    B -->|Code edit request| D[Agent Model Provider]
    B -->|Inline completion| E[Tab Model Provider]
    B -->|Slash command| F[Agent Model Provider]
    
    C --> G[Provider A: Anthropic]
    D --> H[Provider B: OpenAI]
    E --> I[Provider C: Custom / Local]
    
    G --> J[Response]
    H --> J
    I --> J
```

### Routing Rules

1. **Mode determines provider**: Each mode (Chat, Agent, Tab) has its own configured provider
2. **Custom endpoints override built-in**: When a custom endpoint is configured for a mode, it replaces the built-in provider for that mode only
3. **Fallback behavior**: If the configured provider is unavailable, Cursor attempts the next available provider (if configured)
4. **Cloud vs local**: Tab completions may run locally or in the cloud depending on model size and configuration

